{"ts":"2026-09-09T05:47:29+03:00","event":"note","text":"Contradiction recorded rather than resolved, found by the adversarial audit and carried into q10's deferred cycle. Three fields of this sample cannot all be right at once. (a) The L1 justification says in so many words that the numeric coefficients are absent from 736 on and that L1 holds by a single-frame read at 728-735 - but 728-735 lies inside the OPTIONAL window [709.0, 735.4], while the REQUIRED window is [736.7, 772.5], where full_window1.10 confirmed on frames that not a single digit is on screen and the x^4 slot sits inside an ellipsis. By 7.3 the level is that of the cheapest route INCLUDING waiting for the required showing, and at the required showing the route is recall, not reading. That is checklist 4.7 - a window that does not answer its own rubric - the very defect this round caught on q03 and did not apply here. (b) Both triggers carry evidence_span [455.0, 470.0], which says the last evidence is at 470; that is coherent with the values being established there and re-displayed later as corroboration, but it is NOT coherent with 'L1 holds by a read at 728-735'. (c) The derived axis 'post' follows from that span, so if the span is stale the axis is wrong too. Which of the three moves is a measurement question, not a desk one: it needs a fresh full_sample on the reworded question that states, for each rubric item, the earliest moment it is available INSIDE the required window. Until then the level, the span and the axis of q10 are all provisional.","refers_to":"3b1b__3d6DsjIBzJ4__q10"}
