{"ts":"2026-09-09T13:00:50+03:00","event":"note","text":"History repair by note, for a rule that arrived after the events. While this round was closing, coordinator_log.py gained a mandatory --window on --kind boundary (and an optional one on --kind rubric), so that the debt of a boundary edit is full_windowN of the window it touched rather than any window's review - the fix for gap #10 of this round's report. Today's two boundary edits on 3b1b__3d6DsjIBzJ4__q14 were written before that option existed and carry no window field: line 477 (the human's fourth-window edit) touches windows 0 and 1, and line 486 (the consolidation of full_window0.11 and full_window1.11) touches the evidence_span of triggers 0 and 1. Under the new rule they would have been logged as two events each, --window 0 and --window 1. Both windows were in fact reviewed - fw0_r11_q14_p1 and fw1_r11_q14_p2, artifacts full_window0.11.json and full_window1.11.json - so the debt is discharged in substance, and the same holds for the older windowless boundary edits on q02, q03, q04 and q10 earlier in this log. check --final is unaffected: an event without a window keeps the legacy reading, in which any window's review settles it."}
{"ts":"2026-09-09T13:08:55+03:00","event":"note","text":"Warning for whoever reads the artifacts of 3b1b__3d6DsjIBzJ4__q14 next: the window INDICES shifted under the artifact NAMES when the human's fourth window was opened, so the file name no longer says which window a review is about. Before the split the sample had three triggers - 0 = [956.0, 1012.4] (pink and blue), 1 = [1012.5, 1019.5] (yellow), 2 = [1020.0, 1030.9] (required, three items). After it there are four: 0 = [956.0, 987.9] and 1 = [988.0, 1012.4] carry the pink item, 2 = the yellow window, 3 = the required window. So full_window1.10 is the YELLOW window (now idx 2) and full_window2.10 is the REQUIRED window (now idx 3), while full_window1.11 of today is the NEW window 1. All four current windows have been reviewed - 0 and 1 today as full_window0.11 and full_window1.11, 2 as full_window1.10 (PASS), 3 as full_window2.10 (PASS) - and nothing is owed. Recorded so that the next round does not re-review the yellow window believing it to be the required one, or vice versa. The new --window field on sample-edit fixes this going forward for edits, but not for artifact file names.","refers_to":"3b1b__3d6DsjIBzJ4__q14"}
