{"ts":"2026-09-10T00:06:14+03:00","event":"finish","agent":"fw1_r12b_q04","status":"completed","summary":"clean rerun of the required window [272.0, 308.5] with data/reviews closed to it and the workspace at t_end+10: same shape of result as the optional window's clean rerun - four items ok or na, and 2.5 fires mechanically with a no-op proposal. The stream hands over the raw target -1 by 273 and the relation 2c2 by ~302, but the counterfactual construction (double to -2, 2c2 = -2, c2 = -1) is spoken and shown nowhere through 318.5; the author carries the REAL problem to c2 = -1/2 at 311.0, which the rubric already excludes. The residue re-levels to L2, which is the sample's declared level, so the proposal is a confirmation rather than an edit. Also notes, outside its items, that the caption at 311.9-316.6 reads 'c2 itself should be -2' while the frame shows -1/2 - an ASR artifact that could mislead a transcript-only reader","artifact":"data/reviews/3d6DsjIBzJ4/3b1b__3d6DsjIBzJ4__q04/full_window1.12b.json"}
{"ts":"2026-09-10T00:06:14+03:00","event":"finish","agent":"fs_r3_q15","status":"completed","summary":"FIX_QUESTION, one item of twelve: 5.3 discriminator-in-question. 'Replace ONLY its first term by 1/4 WHILE RETAINING that displayed ratio' is self-contradictory - keeping the ratio turns the series into 1/4 + 1/12 + 1/36 + ..., so every term changes and 'only the first term' is literally false. A model resolving the collision the other way (overwrite the first term, leave 1/9, 1/27, 1/81 alone) gets 1/4 + 1/6 = 5/12, i.e. 1/12 below 1/2, and scores zero; nothing in the question breaks the tie and the rubric excludes 1/2 but says nothing about 5/12. Everything else ok or na: the reference answer was recomputed with exact fractions and the on-screen running totals 0.3333333 / 0.4444444 / 0.4814815 / 0.4997714 independently identify which series is being summed; 3.1 is clean because every earlier displayed sum carries a variable and the next numeric series (e^1) appears at 1108, after the window. t_s null (the index puts the series complete at 1076.0 against t_start 1077.0, a one-second gap). Two medium-confidence calls passed to the coordinator: L3 kept because the closed form a/(1-r) is never on screen, and rubric item 4 would be safer as 'the new sum is not 1/2'","artifact":"data/reviews/3d6DsjIBzJ4/3b1b__3d6DsjIBzJ4__q15/full_sample.3.json"}
