{"ts":"2026-09-10T00:44:44+03:00","event":"note","text":"Coordinator error and its repair, 2026-09-10. Doing the section-5 cleanup of consolidated workspaces I wrote the guard as a zsh loop over an unquoted variable holding a list of active agent names - and zsh does not word-split a variable, so the guard matched nothing and all 193 workspaces went, including those of the four agents running at that moment (pt_r4b_q15, fs_r4_q15, fw0_r4_q15, fw1_r13_q10). All four were recreated within a minute at identical bounds with their sample.json restored, and each agent was sent an operational notice to retry any failed read and re-pull dense frames. No artifact and no log line was lost; the only casualty is dense frames some of them may have had to pull twice. This is the SECOND time the same zsh gotcha has broken a workspace loop this round - the first silently prepared no workspaces at all. Rule for anything with rm in it from now on: never iterate a bare variable in this shell, write the list literally or drive it from python"}
