{"ts":"2026-09-10T00:47:50+03:00","event":"note","text":"pt_r4c_q15 supplies an independent corroboration of blind_solved false on q15, and it is worth recording because it is the strongest form the evidence can take. Denied the screen, the opus probe recognised the video as 3Blue1Brown's Taylor series chapter, recalled 'the halving illustration' and instantiated r = 1/2, L = 1, S = 1/2 - flagging it in basis as recollection rather than reading. Every one of those numbers is wrong here: the series is 1/3 + 1/9 + 1/27 + ..., r = 1/3, L = 1/2, S = 3/8. So the natural memory of this exact video, held by a model that correctly identified it, leads away from the answer. That is section 1's counterfactual test passing in the sharpest way available: different screen content would make the recalled answer wrong, and it does"}
